{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"painted-epidermal-shelduck","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Symptom\n\nEvery local `rebar` CLI invocation in the main checkout `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar` emits:\n\n```\nWARNING rebar._store.sync: tickets sync could not auto-merge origin/tickets — local state kept; run: rebar fsck-recover\n```\n\nThe command then succeeds and returns data, so this is a degraded-but-working state, not a hard failure. MCP tracker writes are unaffected — every write this session returned `push_status: {\"state\": \"ok\"}`.\n\n## Observations (facts, not yet interpreted)\n\nMeasured 2026-10-27 ~21:30 PDT:\n\n- `git rev-list --left-right --count tickets...origin/tickets` → **4 ahead, 32 behind**.\n- `git merge-base tickets origin/tickets` → `237b90d370987721aec488df41529715d344af00`. **A common ancestor exists**, so this is NOT the no-common-ancestor `DIVERGED` case that `docs/concurrency.md` describes as refusing the first new write.\n- The 4 local-only commits are, newest first:\n  - `40c378b600d` 20:53:16 `ticket: REBUILD SNAPSHOT 52b0-6a6a-c66b-4c59`\n  - `faa4618083c` 20:03:05 `ticket: REBUILD SNAPSHOT 40a7-7c22-a553-4a1f`\n  - `b115f8b5099` 19:43:57 `ticket: REBUILD SNAPSHOT 14f4-d616-70df-466d`\n  - `465a93c5673` 18:56:20 `ticket: REBUILD SNAPSHOT 075b-1479-dcb7-40ab`\n\n  **All four are `REBUILD SNAPSHOT`** — every one is a derived/compacted artifact, not an original ticket event (no CREATE/EDIT/COMMENT/LINK/TRANSITION among them).\n- Remote-only commits include `ticket: LINK 0ef7-c987-a8d5-4a39` and `ticket: REVIEW_RESULT 0ef7-c987-a8d5-4a39` timestamped 21:22:13-21:22:19 — a ticket this session never touched, so **at least one other agent session was writing the store concurrently**.\n\n## Hypotheses (competing, none yet tested)\n\n1. **Snapshot collision.** Two sessions independently rebuilt a snapshot from different bases; the resulting trees conflict textually, so the auto-merge strategy cannot resolve them. The all-`REBUILD SNAPSHOT` composition of the local-only set is consistent with this but does not establish it.\n2. **Merge strategy gap.** The sync path's auto-merge has no union/ours strategy registered for the snapshot path, so any snapshot divergence — however benign — fails the merge rather than regenerating.\n3. **Unrelated local corruption.** Something else wedged the branch and the snapshot commits are incidental.\n\nThese are untested. Do not fix before distinguishing them.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nIf hypothesis 1 or 2 holds, every host running more than one concurrent agent session will drift into this state routinely, and the operator-facing instruction is a manual `rebar fsck-recover`. A snapshot is rebuildable by definition, so a conflict between two rebuilds of the same derived state should not require human intervention — it should resolve by regenerating.\n\nThe 32-commit backlog also means the local CLI serves **stale reads** while warning only on stderr. An agent using the local CLI carve-out (`verify-commit-ticket`, `review-plan --status`, `rebar explain`) could act on ticket state 32 events behind the store.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Root cause identified and stated with evidence, distinguishing between the hypotheses above — specifically, whether the merge fails because of snapshot content conflict, a missing merge strategy, or something else.\n- [ ] A reproduction exists: two concurrent writers driven to produce the same auto-merge failure, or a documented explanation of why it cannot be reproduced deterministically.\n- [ ] Regression test covering the identified cause.\n- [ ] Remediation: if snapshot conflicts are the cause, the sync path resolves them by regenerating the derived state rather than surfacing an unresolvable merge to the operator.\n- [ ] The main checkout `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar` is returned to a clean sync state. **Do not use `--force` on any surface; if recovery needs one, stop and escalate to the user.** Note that `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar` is a shared checkout that may hold uncommitted operator WIP — do not reset, stash, or fast-forward it destructively.\n- [ ] If the stale-read exposure is real, state whether the warning should become a hard failure for the local-CLI reads that agents are told to use.\n\nDiscovered 2026-10-27 while landing story `6b66-9378-ebb1-446c`.","id":"f1a2-0755-693d-4924","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["tracker","concurrency","store-sync"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Local tickets branch cannot auto-merge origin/tickets; 4 local-only REBUILD SNAPSHOT commits, 32 behind"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793161827870566127,"uuid":"fdab2aa4-2485-44d5-b505-d73e7bfeef3d"}